            "line": 239,
            "title": "Zig fetch work directory is never removed",
            "detail": "newZigFetcher creates a temp directory with os.MkdirTemp and nothing in the diff removes it, so fetched packages build up in the temp directory across runs. This is not a security issue."
          },
          {
            "severity": "info",
            "file": "internal/checksums/archive.go",
            "line": 133,
            "title": "Trailing-data check after tar EOF is bounded by maxArchive",
            "detail": "After the tar end-of-archive marker, the new check reads at most maxArchive bytes and rejects any non-zero byte. Trailing data beyond that limit is not inspected. Most likely the earlier size limits already bound the whole archive, so this is minor."
          },
          {
            "severity": "info",
            "file": "internal/review/zig.go",
            "line": 256,
            "title": "Repository zig-pkg copies are trusted by directory name",
            "detail": "Packages found in the repository's zig-pkg are used without checking them against the pinned hash. They are marked InRepo, though, and so are reviewed whole as vendor code, which matches the stated intent."
